      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two readily obtainable measurements on the admission electrocardiogram-a higher ST-segment elevation in lead III than in lead II and a greater ST-segment depression in lead aVL than in lead I-can distinguish right coronary artery from left circumflex artery-related acute inferior wall myocardial infarction."},
